			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1522979">
									

<p>&#8230; because she was told she had to find the one person who could prove her innocence. This choice of words implies, very strongly, that such a person exists (even if she was unable to find that person), and that therefore she did not actually commit the crime in question.</p>
<p>It's not &quot;find the person who can give you an alibi&quot;, it's not &quot;find the lawyer who can keep you from being convicted&quot;, it's not &quot;find the story that will convince the judge&quot;. It's &quot;find the person who can prove your innocence&quot;.</p>
<p>This is why everyone is upset about mistreating the D-class. Because you've phrased this in such a way that it's obvious she's innocent, and most readers are used to thinking about D-class as criminal scum who deserve whatever happens to them.</p>

